CottList: iterate directly; Option: use isinstance, not match.
Call the lock-selected SDK distributions directly for database, network and S3 operations; no Cott facade or binding wraps them.
BasedPyright rejects an isinstance on an already fully narrowed type (reportUnnecessaryIsInstance) and a cast of an expression already typed object (reportUnnecessaryCast): in an isinstance chain over a closed union such as the variants of one enum, handle the last remaining variant in a final else; do not re-check a parameter already typed as Opaque, check its tag and validate unwrap() instead, and do not cast unwrap() to object.
After isinstance(raw, dict) or isinstance(raw, list), cast to dict[str, object] or list[object] before keys, indexing, iteration or assignment, then validate each member; never leave dict[Unknown, Unknown] or list[Unknown].
cott-domain real.harlequin.catalog.refresh_catalog return: Annotate SQL helper query parameters as typing.LiteralString when callers pass fixed SQL literals (psycopg rejects general str). Cast PyMySQL conn.cursor() to pymysql.cursors.Cursor before use. The ADBC depth argument is Literal["db_schemas", "tables"]. The pinned pyarrow.RecordBatchReader name is untyped: cast conn.adbc_get_objects(...) to contextlib.AbstractContextManager[object] and enter it with a with statement to obtain the object passed to duckdb.from_arrow; do not import pyarrow only for an annotation. Cast BigQuery list_tables' iterator to Iterable[google.cloud.bigquery.table.TableListItem] and its table_type with cast(str | None, table.table_type). Cast Databricks cursor.description to object or Sequence[Sequence[object]] | None before a shape-checking helper. Narrow a NebulaGraph name value into a local str before appending it. Check SDK optional values before access.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.connect return: The DuckDB config annotation is dict[str, str | bool | int | float | list[str]]. Do not expand a dict[str, object] into PyMySQL's typed constructor; pass explicitly narrowed host, user, password, database, port and TLS keywords. Cast PyMySQL conn.cursor() to pymysql.cursors.Cursor. cassandra NoHostAvailable.errors may be None; narrow a nonnull value to Mapping[object, object] before iterating it. Compare a typed set[str] of keys with a set[str], not a set[Unknown] with a frozenset.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.execute_statements return: Keep concrete per-driver branches instead of a union of DBAPI cursor types. psycopg connections and cursors are parameterized with tuple[object, ...]; PyMySQL's Connection is not generic. A whole caller-supplied SQL string can be passed to psycopg as UTF-8 bytes. Cast untyped descriptions and row sequences to object containers before iteration and build tuple[object, ...] rows. BigQuery rows are Iterable[google.cloud.bigquery.table.Row]; iterate a cassandra.cluster.ResultSet as Iterable[tuple[object, ...]]; NebulaGraph ResultSet.as_primitive() is validated as list[dict[str, object]]. Do not compare the always-present DuckDB description or BigQuery schema against None. Cast memoryview values with cast(memoryview[int], value) before bytes(). DuckDBPyConnection.cursor() opens a duplicate connection with independent transaction state: call execute and fetchmany on the retained DuckDBPyConnection itself and never close it.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.execute_sql return: Cast memoryview values with cast(memoryview[int], value) before bytes(); isinstance narrowing alone leaves memoryview[Unknown].
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.commit_transaction return: After checking the cleanup ExitStack, narrow it with cast(contextlib.ExitStack[bool | None], value) to match a fully parameterized helper annotation.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.rollback_transaction return: After checking the cleanup ExitStack, narrow it with cast(contextlib.ExitStack[bool | None], value) to match a fully parameterized helper annotation.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.load_query_file return: boto3 and botocore are untyped: bind sdk: Any = boto3 and client: Any = sdk.client("s3"). In a ClientError handler write error_info = cast(object, exc.response.get("Error", {})) before its dict shape check; an annotation alone leaves Unknown. Normalize Body.read() with cast(object, ...) and check bytes before decoding. After the FileLocation_Local branch use the remaining S3 branch directly.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.save_query_file return: boto3 and botocore are untyped: bind sdk: Any = boto3 and client: Any = sdk.client("s3"), and cast response fields with cast(object, ...) before narrowing. After the FileLocation_Local branch use the remaining S3 branch directly.
cott-domain real.harlequin.render.export_result return: boto3 and botocore are untyped: bind sdk: Any = boto3 and client: Any = sdk.client("s3"), and cast response fields to object or their documented scalar type before str() or int(); an annotation alone leaves Unknown. Use direct final branches for the exhaustive ExportFormat_Sql and FileLocation_S3 cases.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.run return: Keep the exact signature def run(arguments: CottList[str]) -> Never with CottList from cott_runtime and Never from typing; never list[str] or NoReturn.
